75562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475895 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475895 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475895 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475895 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475895 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186475523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475895 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d8937436-576e-5320-a137-6b981c96167e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186475706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475897 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d9d0e6f8-2892-55f4-a237-affcef970729" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475912 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475912 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108434" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475912 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475912 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+s⟨1,0,2⟩+t⟨0,-2,3⟩.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475912 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07e33caa-9650-5834-8d9a-46cc82f723d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475912 #edb/ref 1074 "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,2⟩\\times ⟨0,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =4i-3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨4,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =⟨5,3,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+3w,-1+4w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ 4(1+3w)-3(-1+4w)-2(2-w) & =19 \\\\ 4+12w+3-12w-4+2w & =19 \\\\ 2w & =16 \\\\ w & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=8$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1+3(8),-1+4(8),2-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨25,31,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(25,31,-6).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475922 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475922 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108336" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475922 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475922 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2+t \\\\ y=-1+3t \\\\ z=3-2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x+y-5z=63.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475922 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "231a9d15-2430-5e82-a7fa-b3cd0ec4e91a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475922 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-5z & =63 \\\\ 2(2+t)+(-1+3t)-5(3-2t) & =63 \\\\ 4+2t-1+3t-15+10t & =63 \\\\ 15t & =75 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2+5=7 \\\\ y=-1+3(5)=14 \\\\ z=3-2(5)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(7,14,-7).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475933 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475933 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108370" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475933 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475933 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-7⟩+t⟨4,-3,2⟩,\\,Π:5x+2y-7z-15=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475933 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "42cfce4b-bf3d-5d7e-8fad-15e0c813875c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475933 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2y-7z-15 & =0 \\\\ 5x+2y-7z & =15 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ 5(5+4t)+2(3-3t)-7(-7+2t) & =15 \\\\ 25+20t+6-6t+49-14t & =15 \\\\ 80 & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475938 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475938 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475938 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475938 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,4,-1⟩+t⟨1,4,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩=45.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475938 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6079a48b-0752-583a-8f2a-84194653fec2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475938 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩ & =45 \\\\ ⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩ & =45 \\\\ 3(2+t)+12(4+4t)+9(-1+3t) & =45 \\\\ 6+3t+48+48t-9+27t & =45 \\\\ 78t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(0),4+4(0),-1+3(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(2,4,-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475941 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475941 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74001" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475941 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475941 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-3-7t \\\\ z=1-2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:-2x+4y-7z=17.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475941 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "789a0f9b-548a-5d80-a6d7-b592e86b7749" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475941 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y-7z & =17 \\\\ -2(2-3t)+4(-3-7t)-7(1-2t) & =17 \\\\ -4+6t-12-28t-7+14t & =17 \\\\ -8t & =40 \\\\ t & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3(-5)=17 \\\\ y=-3-7(-5)=32 \\\\ z=1-2(-5)=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(17,32,11).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475947 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475947 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475947 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475947 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-2⟩+t⟨3,-1,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩=8.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475947 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ef5750d-a5da-50af-8419-8b1661dfe47b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475947 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5+3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5+3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩ & =8 \\\\ ⟨5-3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩ & =8 \\\\ -2(5+3t)+4(3-t)+5\\cdot (-2+2t) & =8 \\\\ -10-6t+12-4t-10+10t & =8 \\\\ -8 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475955 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475955 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475955 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475955 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=8+5t \\\\ z=-7-4t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-3y+z-94=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475955 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b3b4f2c0-7489-5ff6-9c21-54c57d280888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475955 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z-94 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-3(8+5t)-7-4t & =94 \\\\ 10-4t-24-15t-7-4t & =94 \\\\ -23t & =115 \\\\ t & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-5)=15 \\\\ y=8+5(-5)=-17 \\\\ z=-7-4(-5)=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(15,-17,13).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475975 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33082" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475975 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475975 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,1⟩+w⟨-3,-2,3⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-15,1,1⟩+s⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨1,4,0⟩.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475975 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4fbd5e6-b819-591a-880c-a933bdaba9d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475975 #edb/ref 1074 "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩\\times ⟨1,4,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-8i+2j+8k \\\\  & =⟨-8,2,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =⟨-15,1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2,3,1⟩+w⟨-3,-2,3⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130 \\\\ ⟨2-3w,3-2w,1+3w⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130 \\\\ -8(2-3w)+2(3-2w)+8(1+3w) & =130 \\\\ -16+24w+6-4w+8+24w & =130 \\\\ 44w & =132 \\\\ w & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨2-3(3),3-2(3),1+3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,-3,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-7,-3,10).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
